It is a warm Saturday afternoon in May.
My shift at the café is over.
"Bye, Elif, see you next weekend!" I say.
Then I travel back to the flat.
The sun is shining and the sky is blue.
My thick winter coat is hanging right at the back of the wardrobe.
I do not need it anymore now.
But I look at my other clothes.
I am not ready for the summer yet.
My jumpers are too warm.
I absolutely need a thin summer jacket.
It is much lighter than a winter jacket.
I also want to buy a new shirt.
I still have a lot of time today.
The weather is perfect for a trip into town.
I pack my wallet into the backpack.
Then I go back outside.
